) versus modest pro-Evans support", "Evans holds a large cash-on-hand edge but faces a tough national environment"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Democratic edge in a zero-PVI district with a favorable environment, and most raters call the seat Lean D or a flip, while markets price Rutinel well ahead. The lone poll, from a Republican-leaning pollster, shows a tied race, so the margin stays modest rather than runaway.", "watch": "Any new independent polling showing Evans holding or gaining ground, or a shift in the national environment, could move this back toward a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Gabe Evans (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Colorado's 8th District is a pure battleground, with no partisan lean in its fundamentals. First-term Republican Gabe Evans is defending the seat against Democrat Manny Rutinel in what raters widely view as a top flip opportunity, with most calling it Lean D or a tossup. Prediction markets give Rutinel roughly a 75-87% chance of winning.\n\nEvans has raised more than $5 million and holds a large cash-on-hand advantage, but Rutinel benefits from about $3.5 million in outside support and a favorable national climate. The only public poll, conducted by a Republican-leaning firm, shows the race essentially tied, suggesting the contest remains competitive despite the Democratic tilt in ratings and markets.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7882, "margin": 4.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7652, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7649, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7806, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7027, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6862, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7621, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7968, "margin": 4.5}]}